Two crash fixes from the Mac's orbslam_ws/src/ORB_SLAM3 (2026-10-18, commit 8b16355d there), applied to ~/objpose/ORB_SLAM3_src
on 2026-10-18 19:00 on top of 03 (paper_etrij_261003 doc 30 section 4.2):
  MapPoint::ComputeDistinctiveDescriptors: N x N distance array moved from the stack to the heap (SIGBUS on 512 KB macOS thread stacks)
  LocalMapping::Release(): no longer deletes queued keyframes, one of which can already be in the map (use-after-free in ResetActiveMap)
  cd ORB_SLAM3 && patch -p1 < 04-orbslam3-crash-fixes-261018.patch

diff -ruN a/src/LocalMapping.cc b/src/LocalMapping.cc
--- a/src/LocalMapping.cc	2026-10-18 19:09:05
+++ b/src/LocalMapping.cc	2026-10-18 19:09:05
@@ -863,8 +863,9 @@
         return;
     mbStopped = false;
     mbStopRequested = false;
-    for(list<KeyFrame*>::iterator lit = mlNewKeyFrames.begin(), lend=mlNewKeyFrames.end(); lit!=lend; lit++)
-        delete *lit;
+    // Drop the queue but do not delete: a queued keyframe can already be in the map (the RGB-D/stereo initial KF is
+    // added by Tracking before it is queued) and Tracking/MapPoints still point to it. Deleting it left a dangling
+    // pointer in Map::mspKeyFrames, and the next ResetActiveMap -> Map::clear() locked a freed mutex (OpenLORIS corridor).
     mlNewKeyFrames.clear();
 
     cout << "Local Mapping RELEASE" << endl;
